# PHILO-3-02 D2 — documented base install after fix

This repeats the README source install in a new venv with an isolated HOME.
No `dev`, `test`, or `meeting` extra was requested.  The global uv cache was
used only to avoid redundant downloads; the package environment and HOME are
fresh.  No hub, model, endpoint, microphone, keychain, or desk was started.

Command:

```sh
install_home=$(mktemp -d)
install_venv=$(mktemp -d)
export HOME="$install_home"
export PATH=/Users/karol/.nvm/versions/node/v22.21.0/bin:$PATH
export UV_CACHE_DIR=/Users/karol/Library/Caches/uv
printf '%s\n' "HOME=$HOME" "VENV=$install_venv" "INSTALL=uv pip install -e ."
uv venv "$install_venv"
source "$install_venv/bin/activate"
uv pip install -e .
python - <<'PY'
from importlib import metadata
import importlib.util

print(f"holdspeak distribution: {metadata.version('holdspeak')}")
for name in ('holdspeak', 'openai', 'llama_cpp', 'resemblyzer', 'zeroconf'):
    spec = importlib.util.find_spec(name)
    print(f"{name}: {spec.origin if spec else 'MISSING'}")
PY
python -c 'from holdspeak.intel import OpenAI; print(f"OpenAI={OpenAI!r}"); assert OpenAI is not None, "production OpenAI client is unavailable"'
```

